    "rich_text_czWEgw": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_kYqBzH": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Diamond Buying Guide: How to Choose the Right Diamond",
            "use_h1": true
          }
        },
        "text_jUByfz": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Buying a diamond is a significant decision—whether for an engagement ring, a gift, or a personal investment. Understanding how diamonds are graded and what factors influence their value helps you make a confident and informed choice.</p><p>At Milano Jewelry, we focus on transparency, offering both natural and lab-grown diamonds that are certified and carefully selected for quality.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        },
        "subheading_JXaHAf": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "What Are the 4Cs of Diamonds?"
          }
        },
        "text_hNnGUx": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The 4Cs—Cut, Color, Clarity, and Carat Weight—are the global standard for evaluating diamond quality.</p><p>These four factors determine a diamond’s appearance, value, and overall appeal.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        },
        "subheading_Ncnjjt": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Diamond Cut: The Most Important Factor"
          }
        },
        "text_wCkTi3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The cut of a diamond refers to how well it has been shaped and polished. It directly affects how light reflects within the stone, determining its brilliance and sparkle.</p><h3>Cut Grades:</h3><ul><li><strong>Ideal Cut</strong>: Maximum brilliance and light performance<br/></li><li><strong>Very Good Cut</strong>: High sparkle with slight variations<br/></li><li><strong>Good Cut</strong>: Moderate brilliance with less light reflection<br/></li><li><strong>Fair to Poor Cut</strong>: Reduced sparkle and visual appeal<br/></li></ul><p>A well-cut diamond will appear brighter and more refined, even if other factors are lower.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_kYqBzH",
