    "rich_text_JyMWB8": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "subheading_N3jcVD": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Diamond Color: Understanding the Scale"
          }
        },
        "text_E9GHmB": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Clarity measures the presence of internal inclusions or surface blemishes within a diamond.</p><h3>Clarity Grades:</h3><ul><li><strong>FL / IF</strong>: No visible inclusions under magnification<br/></li><li><strong>VVS1 / VVS2</strong>: Extremely minor inclusions<br/></li><li><strong>VS1 / VS2</strong>: Minor inclusions, not visible to the naked eye<br/></li><li><strong>SI1 / SI2</strong>: Noticeable inclusions, sometimes visible<br/></li><li><strong>I1–I3</strong>: Obvious inclusions affecting appearance<br/></li></ul><p>Many diamonds in the VS and SI range offer excellent visual clarity without unnecessary cost.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        },
